WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:03.680
January 1983

2
00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:13.840
Part VI
Independence Day

3
00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:21.920
Oh boy.

4
00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:23.800
What's up?

5
00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:31.160
You won't believe the nightmare
I saw last night.

6
00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:33.960
Magomajev won our
a local singing contest?

7
00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:38.400
That's impossible!
- How could I know what you saw.

8
00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:41.000
What?
- Tell me what you saw?

9
00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:46.400
I come home from work,
two bricks in my bag, as usual.

10
00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:49.720
And suddenly I see,

11
00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:56.040
that there's the blue-white-black
flag on my home building.

12
00:00:56.480 --> 00:00:59.120
What?
- My thoughts exactly.

13
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:03.560
I see the housekeeper,
who's sweeping the street.

14
00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:06.320
I ask him, how is it possible

15
00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:11.840
that there's a tricolor publicly
displayed in broad daylight.

16
00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:15.880
What did he say?
- He didn't understand the question.

17
00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:21.840
Apparently Estonian Republic
had been free for years,

18
00:01:22.120 --> 00:01:27.560
and not only free, but
a member of the NATO.

19
00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:31.960
Can you imagine that?
- No, no I can't.

20
00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:35.680
I was completely shocked.
- Didn't you feel happy?

21
00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:37.640
How could I?

22
00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:44.800
See, I've spent a lifetime
waiting for the Estonian Republic.

23
00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:49.040
And now I have two bricks in my bag.
- So?

24
00:01:49.240 --> 00:01:57.520
Don't you understand?
I wasn't stealing bricks from Russia,

25
00:01:57.880 --> 00:02:00.320
but from free Estonia.

26
00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:04.200
Doesn't matter it was in a dream.

27
00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:46.080
What's wrong?
- Our whole family, can't stand them!

28
00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:52.520
What's the problem?
- They're a bunch of greedy

29
00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:56.120
and selfish thieves.
- Pille?

30
00:02:56.240 --> 00:02:58.800
I can't stand it any more.
- What exactly?

31
00:02:58.880 --> 00:03:00.400
The Russian business.

32
00:03:01.880 --> 00:03:06.120
The Paul Street boys!
Show me one person who does.

33
00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:12.600
Pille, silly girl, thanks to the USSR,
our family is much better off than

34
00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:18.000
a lot of other families.
Think where our mother works at.

35
00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:21.560
Exactly.
She's milking the state non-stop!

36
00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:24.360
That's what the state is for!

37
00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:28.280
That's perceived inevitability.

38
00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:32.600
Where did that come from?
- I read things...

39
00:03:32.680 --> 00:03:35.640
"Agu Sihvka Reports" and
car repairman's handbook.

40
00:04:04.280 --> 00:04:07.000
Jüri, what are you doing?

41
00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:11.840
Assembling a Kalashnikov
blindfolded.

42
00:04:16.280 --> 00:04:18.920
From what?
- From what I could find.

43
00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:22.480
Stop the nonsense.

44
00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:27.480
I want to know what is what.

45
00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:29.600
What do you mean?

46
00:04:31.560 --> 00:04:36.040
Whether I recognize which part
goes where without seeing them.

47
00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:39.080
It's the Red Army Day tomorrow,
I have to get in shape

48
00:04:39.160 --> 00:04:40.040
for the competitions.

49
00:04:40.120 --> 00:04:43.120
Go somewhere else, can't you see
I'm desperate here?

50
00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:45.960
Of course not, my eyes are covered.

51
00:04:47.560 --> 00:04:53.200
Quickly, make way! Let me past!
Time to make the day count!

52
00:04:53.280 --> 00:04:56.280
How dare you! I was next!

53
00:04:57.320 --> 00:04:59.560
Come out, right now!

54
00:05:00.680 --> 00:05:02.880
Mom, where are you?
- In queue!

55
00:05:03.640 --> 00:05:08.040
You are despicable, hear me?
You're not even registered here!

56
00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:11.920
I will complain, I will!
- Go right ahead!

57
00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:14.920
Just make sure you
don't leave a trail!

58
00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:22.400
I'll take the scarf off now.

59
00:05:25.400 --> 00:05:27.000
I'll go to the basement now.

60
00:05:27.080 --> 00:05:30.120
Why there?
- You told me when I was little

61
00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:34.680
that when I hear harmonica
I should run - fascists are coming!

62
00:05:37.280 --> 00:05:42.480
What's this?
- Smell it. Finnish soap!

63
00:05:42.840 --> 00:05:44.320
Bought from Alex.

64
00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:48.400
Then wash yourself.
You reek of beer and sweat.

65
00:05:48.680 --> 00:05:51.360
With Finnish soap?
- What, isn't that good enough?

66
00:05:51.840 --> 00:05:55.800
Finnish soap is for selling.
- You plan to rip someone off again!

67
00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:58.720
No, I'll swap it.
- For what?

68
00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:04.160
For freedom. The master promised
me a day off if I got him that.

69
00:06:04.640 --> 00:06:10.720
He has a date tomorrow,
hopes it'll help him score.

70
00:06:14.680 --> 00:06:18.560
But even Finnish soap won't help him.
- Why?

71
00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:23.480
The guy constantly smells
of gasoline and garlic.

72
00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:27.920
I'm going to study humanities.

73
00:06:35.640 --> 00:06:37.040
Enter!

74
00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:43.320
Hello! Where's Sirje?
I have an urgent matter with her.

75
00:06:43.680 --> 00:06:45.880
Come in quickly and close the door!

76
00:06:52.680 --> 00:06:55.920
What do you mean in a collective farm?
Why did the Vokk-hag send her there?

77
00:06:56.080 --> 00:07:01.320
Sirje went to present a red flag.
Something happened on their way back.

78
00:07:01.680 --> 00:07:04.040
The chauffeur called, car's broken.

79
00:07:04.120 --> 00:07:07.200
An accident!
- Sirje's fine.

80
00:07:07.480 --> 00:07:11.200
Someone else isn't?
- That's exactly it.

81
00:07:11.560 --> 00:07:14.760
That's a big problem then.
- Not quite, because...

82
00:07:19.480 --> 00:07:21.080
A happy accident.

83
00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:32.440
I'm doing... not so well.
- What's wrong?

84
00:07:32.760 --> 00:07:34.960
I wanted to borrow 50 rubles,

85
00:07:35.040 --> 00:07:37.520
or once in a lifetime chance
will slip away.

86
00:07:38.040 --> 00:07:42.280
I'm afraid I can't help you out.
- No, that's not what I meant.

87
00:07:42.520 --> 00:07:46.640
Otherwise, I wouldn't hesitate,
but I just bought an iron,

88
00:07:46.720 --> 00:07:51.920
curling tongs and an electric drill.
For exchange, you know.

89
00:07:52.000 --> 00:07:55.120
I got an traveling permit
from the union.

90
00:07:56.200 --> 00:07:59.800
Lucky you!
- Of course. I am the union.

91
00:08:00.760 --> 00:08:03.240
A friend offered
me some work for 50 rubles.

92
00:08:03.680 --> 00:08:05.640
I could make an extra 10 rubles
every day,

93
00:08:05.720 --> 00:08:08.880
in addition to the monthly salary.
- Are you going to be a cosmonaut?

94
00:08:08.960 --> 00:08:12.720
No, no, these feet
will stay on the ground.

95
00:08:12.920 --> 00:08:18.640
But I can give you diet coupons for
100 rubles.

96
00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:21.760
You'll pay me back later.

97
00:08:23.760 --> 00:08:28.160
What am I supposed to do with those?
- I, as the leader of the union,

98
00:08:28.320 --> 00:08:34.600
will grant Sirje coupons for diet food.
Diagnose: chronic gastritis.

99
00:08:35.520 --> 00:08:41.000
You can find all kinds of rare food in
the diet diner.

100
00:08:41.960 --> 00:08:46.080
And if you sell these coupons for
even half of their worth,

101
00:08:46.160 --> 00:08:48.480
you'll get the 50 rubles.

102
00:08:48.600 --> 00:08:52.280
You can do that?
- And I'll get 100 rubles.

103
00:08:52.520 --> 00:08:56.840
You devil!
- Not a word to Sirje!

104
00:09:04.040 --> 00:09:06.320
Where do we put it?
- Quiet! There!

105
00:09:12.680 --> 00:09:15.880
Hang it up or cut it up?
- Shh, we've neighbors.

106
00:09:16.040 --> 00:09:19.880
We're screwed if they find out.
Not a single drop of blood!

107
00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:25.480
Okay, give me a sharp blade and
half an hour, and we're done.

108
00:09:27.880 --> 00:09:31.600
Could I have something on?
An apron or something.

109
00:09:40.520 --> 00:09:41.560
Ah, that's fine.

110
00:09:42.440 --> 00:09:44.760
I'll lift it up, you move that rag.

111
00:09:44.880 --> 00:09:46.280
Shh, quiet.

112
00:09:51.160 --> 00:09:52.760
From this side.

113
00:10:11.000 --> 00:10:14.080
That's the backstrap.
- Good, we can fit more in here.

114
00:10:15.600 --> 00:10:17.080
Liver comes next.

115
00:10:21.800 --> 00:10:23.120
Here.

116
00:10:25.040 --> 00:10:26.440
The other side too.

117
00:10:36.600 --> 00:10:37.840
Some more.

118
00:10:44.800 --> 00:10:46.480
Should I put it in here?

119
00:11:01.120 --> 00:11:03.280
Don't scare me like that!

120
00:11:03.360 --> 00:11:05.520
What's going on here?
- We hit a goat.

121
00:11:05.680 --> 00:11:07.960
Couldn't let the meat go to waste.

122
00:11:08.360 --> 00:11:12.640
Hello! I'm Sirje's school mate,

123
00:11:12.800 --> 00:11:15.480
head of the collective farm
"Stepping towards victory".

124
00:11:15.640 --> 00:11:16.720
Aadolf.

125
00:11:16.880 --> 00:11:19.200
Karnats. Rein Karnats.

126
00:11:20.280 --> 00:11:23.760
A bit ironic, don't you think?

127
00:11:24.560 --> 00:11:27.040
What are you doing here?
Why aren't you at home?

128
00:11:27.120 --> 00:11:29.920
It's the independence day tomorrow.

129
00:11:30.200 --> 00:11:33.080
I want to hear
what the Free Europe says.

130
00:11:33.240 --> 00:11:37.680
I need you to go home for a bit.
This meat won't fit into our fridge.

131
00:11:37.800 --> 00:11:42.760
Get your case, take out the bricks.
- I can fill it up again.

132
00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:46.040
I like this man!
- Keep your voices down.

133
00:11:47.600 --> 00:11:50.560
Red, almost blood red from
the outside,

134
00:11:50.640 --> 00:11:53.720
but heart's in the right place.
But another kind of man

135
00:11:53.800 --> 00:11:56.320
could not be the head of a
collective farm, could he?

136
00:11:56.400 --> 00:12:01.040
True. The heart, however,
went onto ice.

137
00:12:04.240 --> 00:12:08.360
I'll give you some ribs too.
- Awesome, thank you!

138
00:12:12.440 --> 00:12:13.960
Two.
- Great!

139
00:12:18.920 --> 00:12:21.000
But I'm not going right away.

140
00:12:21.560 --> 00:12:24.680
Why not?
- We need a toast first!

141
00:12:29.800 --> 00:12:33.400
Estonia was accepted to the
great family of the Soviet Union

142
00:12:33.520 --> 00:12:37.200
as an equal member.
Comrade Mailov,

143
00:12:37.320 --> 00:12:40.080
what would you like to say
on this grand day?

144
00:12:46.320 --> 00:12:50.680
Damn it, I don't want to hear
this red nonsense any more.

145
00:12:55.960 --> 00:12:59.240
Let's drink to
Kuperjanov's memory instead!

146
00:13:01.560 --> 00:13:04.960
And to the hope that rural Estonia
will become as prosperous

147
00:13:05.080 --> 00:13:08.000
as Kirov's collective fish farm.
- Are you mocking me?

148
00:13:08.360 --> 00:13:11.680
No, I mean it!
- A tomato!

149
00:13:14.200 --> 00:13:18.120
What?
- Initially I thought you're a radish.

150
00:13:18.320 --> 00:13:20.400
Red from the outside,
white inside.

151
00:13:20.880 --> 00:13:23.880
But your a full-blown tomato!
- Dad, stop it.

152
00:13:24.440 --> 00:13:27.400
Collective farm system
isn't Rein's fault.

153
00:13:30.520 --> 00:13:34.120
Kirov's collective fish farm,
So called exemplary farm.

154
00:13:34.200 --> 00:13:37.160
Its kindergartens, schools and
retirement homes were obligatory

155
00:13:37.240 --> 00:13:40.800
sightseeing destinations
for the majority of foreign visitors,

156
00:13:40.880 --> 00:13:44.080
to show that everybody in ENSV
are enjoying a good life.

157
00:13:44.160 --> 00:13:47.360
The advancement of now prosperous
Viimsi parish began from there.

158
00:13:47.440 --> 00:13:50.200
It was a rural exception
that proved the rule.

159
00:13:53.080 --> 00:13:56.560
Lately, we've been growing mainly
beetroot.

160
00:13:56.640 --> 00:14:02.000
He dared to compare Kuperjanov
to Kirov, damn it.

161
00:14:02.600 --> 00:14:05.640
Rein, pay him no mind,
he's like that all the time.

162
00:14:09.320 --> 00:14:11.960
You have no idea
where I just came from.

163
00:14:14.720 --> 00:14:16.760
Hello!
- Good day!

164
00:14:17.640 --> 00:14:18.960
Hello, Ats!

165
00:14:19.160 --> 00:14:23.480
Hi!
You can't imagine what just happened!

166
00:14:23.760 --> 00:14:26.440
Did you get a new ticket with the
sports lottery?

167
00:14:26.640 --> 00:14:28.880
I found 50 rubles outside our gate.

168
00:14:28.960 --> 00:14:32.080
What a unusual luck!
- 50 rubles? Lucky!

169
00:14:32.240 --> 00:14:34.440
Naturally!
- Did someone bribe you?

170
00:14:35.160 --> 00:14:38.840
I ran back to town, to a diner.
Bought everything I could

171
00:14:38.920 --> 00:14:42.640
for the diet coupons. Oranges,
orange juice, even paté!

172
00:14:43.800 --> 00:14:48.240
What diet coupons?
You're unemployed, who gave you those?

173
00:14:50.120 --> 00:14:57.320
Someone I know. His stomach is
very bad, he's fed through a tube.

174
00:14:58.640 --> 00:15:01.880
Is going to a sanitarium tomorrow,
gave me the coupons,

175
00:15:01.960 --> 00:15:03.800
so they'd not go to waste.

176
00:15:03.920 --> 00:15:10.040
I'd never pick up Russian ruble,
every man should carry proper money.

177
00:15:10.160 --> 00:15:13.600
Nonsense, you borrowed 2 rubles
from me only yesterday.

178
00:15:15.520 --> 00:15:21.800
Not the Russian money,
I mean this one.

179
00:15:22.120 --> 00:15:23.640
Dear lord, why?

180
00:15:24.440 --> 00:15:28.280
Perhaps Estonia becomes free again.
I'd have the money right away!

181
00:15:29.000 --> 00:15:31.640
It's really not my business,
but aren't you afraid

182
00:15:31.760 --> 00:15:33.680
that the rubles will defile that?

183
00:15:38.400 --> 00:15:40.720
I'm not speaking to a tomato!

184
00:15:57.960 --> 00:16:03.560
Look, Jüri. It has to be!
I think it is.

185
00:16:05.200 --> 00:16:06.760
Could be jam.

186
00:16:06.840 --> 00:16:09.760
Can't you tell the difference between
blood and jam?

187
00:16:10.040 --> 00:16:12.800
We have bloodhounds for that.
And a laboratory.

188
00:16:13.120 --> 00:16:14.560
Taste it.

189
00:16:17.040 --> 00:16:18.400
I checked everything.

190
00:16:19.280 --> 00:16:27.200
It begins from the gate and ends here
or vice versa.

191
00:16:28.240 --> 00:16:29.960
What are your conclusions?

192
00:16:32.600 --> 00:16:33.920
It's not jam.

193
00:16:34.160 --> 00:16:37.680
See! That means that someone
has been killed.

194
00:16:38.120 --> 00:16:41.920
Why do you think that?
- Open your eyes, Jüri.

195
00:16:42.360 --> 00:16:44.600
Think what's going on in the house.

196
00:16:45.520 --> 00:16:48.080
I bet Sirje's new man
got to the old one.

197
00:16:49.520 --> 00:16:51.720
Killed the comrade blue-water captain.

198
00:16:58.280 --> 00:17:02.680
Many of us spend their
summer vacation on the sea.

199
00:17:03.760 --> 00:17:08.840
ENSV lifeguards' training ship “Laine”
is on a roll again.

200
00:17:09.240 --> 00:17:14.400
Saloon, pool, restaurant, bar,
also cultural and sports equipment

201
00:17:14.520 --> 00:17:17.000
are at passengers' disposal.

202
00:17:17.600 --> 00:17:24.080
The best men on board are
the second mechanic Äkplom Oke and...

203
00:17:27.160 --> 00:17:29.720
we have a number of
young and good men.

204
00:17:33.040 --> 00:17:34.600
What next?

205
00:17:39.240 --> 00:17:40.920
Let's do it and go the sleep.

206
00:17:41.000 --> 00:17:43.360
I mean what will become of our life?

207
00:17:46.880 --> 00:17:50.480
What's there to think.
Fridge's full of food.

208
00:17:51.320 --> 00:17:54.400
What are you worried about?
- What happens tomorrow?

209
00:17:54.720 --> 00:17:56.920
We'll eat some meat in the morning,

210
00:17:57.000 --> 00:17:59.760
go to work, come back,
and eat more meat.

211
00:17:59.880 --> 00:18:01.920
That's not a normal life.

212
00:18:07.640 --> 00:18:09.440
You have to divorce Villem.

213
00:18:13.600 --> 00:18:21.440
By the way, I may get a new job,
at the copying center.

214
00:18:22.360 --> 00:18:25.960
What's your job there?
- Fill orders during day time

215
00:18:26.160 --> 00:18:28.480
and copy Finnish TV programs
at night.

216
00:18:31.720 --> 00:18:36.440
Duplicated Finnish TV-programs.
Fairly common during Soviet times.

217
00:18:36.560 --> 00:18:39.920
Thanks to the state institutions
typists' secret hobby,

218
00:18:40.080 --> 00:18:43.920
ordinary people knew
what the Finns were going to show.

219
00:18:44.480 --> 00:18:48.320
Mainly for Tallinners,
the rest of Estonia didn't see

220
00:18:48.480 --> 00:18:51.280
western stations even in their dreams.

221
00:18:53.040 --> 00:18:59.080
Stop sounding like Paavo!
- His copies cost 10 kopecks a piece,

222
00:18:59.240 --> 00:19:05.120
mine will be 15, but I offer quality.
All the titles will be legible.

223
00:19:05.320 --> 00:19:09.800
Fine, suit yourself.
It's great that you found a job.

224
00:19:10.520 --> 00:19:13.160
Okay, let's do it,
I want to go to sleep.

225
00:19:16.920 --> 00:19:19.720
Capital of Turkmen SSR?
- Ashgabat.

226
00:19:20.240 --> 00:19:25.520
Correct, your turn.
- Name an Ukrainian coal mine.

227
00:19:25.680 --> 00:19:33.760
Donetsk... or Donbass.
No, Donetsk. Donbass.

228
00:19:34.880 --> 00:19:38.120
Why do we have to play this game
every evening.

229
00:20:19.080 --> 00:20:24.520
Mom, you could be right.
If there's a body in this house,

230
00:20:24.680 --> 00:20:28.160
it can only be captain's.
Everybody else are asleep.

231
00:20:30.720 --> 00:20:31.640
Listen!

232
00:20:31.800 --> 00:20:33.000
What?

233
00:20:33.640 --> 00:20:34.920
Someone's snoring.

234
00:20:36.960 --> 00:20:38.240
Where?

235
00:20:38.720 --> 00:20:42.440
This means only one thing.
The snorer shouldn't be here.

236
00:20:47.560 --> 00:20:52.320
Who is he?
- The hired killer. Check for ID.

237
00:21:04.240 --> 00:21:05.480
Damn it!

238
00:21:14.320 --> 00:21:17.440
Dear lord, dear lord!

239
00:21:20.760 --> 00:21:23.800
Bloody retards! Shit!

240
00:21:30.680 --> 00:21:31.920
Bunch of animals.

241
00:21:49.560 --> 00:21:55.520
First of all,
the leader of this contest

242
00:21:55.600 --> 00:21:59.800
a potato brought by Rudolf Poom
from Kuusiku test base

243
00:22:00.040 --> 00:22:06.360
has been challenged.
Mickey Mouse is easily recognizable.

244
00:22:06.960 --> 00:22:13.960
However, I doubt that anyone has seen
a cucumber that's 1.5 m long.

245
00:22:21.680 --> 00:22:24.320
I have no idea what they thought.

246
00:22:24.640 --> 00:22:29.080
The neighbors,
usually they are normal people.

247
00:22:29.520 --> 00:22:34.000
I'm a normal person too.
But I don't like to be searched,

248
00:22:34.280 --> 00:22:36.240
especially while I'm asleep.

249
00:22:38.120 --> 00:22:41.080
But we have a problem...
- They stole something?

250
00:22:41.240 --> 00:22:42.080
If only.

251
00:22:43.000 --> 00:22:46.240
The one you punched lights out on,
that was a cop.

252
00:22:47.080 --> 00:22:54.920
A militsiya? A real one?
- Every inch.

253
00:23:03.000 --> 00:23:11.640
How many years do they give for that?
- It's not that bad. We'll fix it.

254
00:23:11.760 --> 00:23:14.840
They're greedy people,
offer them something.

255
00:23:15.280 --> 00:23:16.480
Like what?

256
00:23:17.600 --> 00:23:19.560
You manage a collective farm.

257
00:23:20.440 --> 00:23:23.440
Offer something you have,
a bag of potatoes...

258
00:23:24.280 --> 00:23:25.840
Would that be sufficient?

259
00:23:26.840 --> 00:23:28.240
Two bags!

260
00:23:28.840 --> 00:23:33.240
Two bags of potatoes.
And 5 kg of pork fat and...

261
00:23:33.360 --> 00:23:34.800
It's a deal.

262
00:23:37.760 --> 00:23:43.000
Tell your son to be more careful.
Rein used to box.

263
00:23:45.640 --> 00:23:48.960
My son won't be able to look
around for some time.

264
00:23:49.160 --> 00:23:54.400
These are for you, for the scare.
So we have a deal?

265
00:23:54.520 --> 00:23:56.640
You bet.
- Bet what?

266
00:23:59.040 --> 00:24:00.440
Foreman's word.

267
00:24:00.800 --> 00:24:02.400
The sooner, the better.

268
00:24:08.640 --> 00:24:11.920
Greedy, but still a human.
Gave me flowers and everything.

269
00:24:12.160 --> 00:24:16.480
Pioneers brought them yesterday,
his father's a vet.

270
00:24:16.960 --> 00:24:18.520
It was the Army Day yesterday.

271
00:24:18.600 --> 00:24:21.600
In any case
I'm not taking lawn to countryside.

272
00:24:25.480 --> 00:24:27.800
Thank you so much for the help!

273
00:24:31.240 --> 00:24:32.720
Thank you, Sirje, dear.

274
00:24:34.640 --> 00:24:36.440
Come visit us!

275
00:25:14.200 --> 00:25:16.760
I can't take another bite.
Full to the brim.

276
00:25:16.880 --> 00:25:20.120
Eat, eat! We don't get this stuff
every day.

277
00:25:20.320 --> 00:25:22.840
It's like the diet diner in here.

278
00:25:22.960 --> 00:25:26.600
Darn, what a diet.
I've put away 5 kg of meat.

279
00:25:26.680 --> 00:25:30.560
Drink up! Father went through
a lot of trouble to get it all.

280
00:25:32.800 --> 00:25:34.080
Stepfather.

281
00:25:35.520 --> 00:25:40.920
What are you celebrating?
Bourgeois Estonia's independence day?

282
00:25:43.920 --> 00:25:47.320
How should we know when to
celebrate that? How do you know?

283
00:25:47.440 --> 00:25:50.400
One must know their enemy.
- Sorry, did you have any business?

284
00:25:50.480 --> 00:25:51.520
Paavo!

285
00:25:52.520 --> 00:25:54.240
I came to borrow a rag.

286
00:25:54.720 --> 00:25:59.400
Nikifor needs a compress.
And little boy's eyes too.

287
00:25:59.520 --> 00:26:00.640
Little boy.

288
00:26:00.760 --> 00:26:03.360
Mom, I can't eat
when that woman stares that.

289
00:26:04.080 --> 00:26:06.600
There should be a rag under the sink.

290
00:26:33.560 --> 00:26:36.400
Paavo, Paavo. She should stop ogling
then.

291
00:26:45.760 --> 00:26:49.000
Hello, is this the militsiya?
- Yes.

292
00:26:50.360 --> 00:26:53.560
I'm calling from Vabaduse road,
house No 88.

293
00:26:54.080 --> 00:26:58.760
My neighbors are hannibals.
- Did they cross the mountains

294
00:26:58.840 --> 00:27:01.680
on elephants?
- Did what with elephants?

295
00:27:01.840 --> 00:27:05.520
Cross the mountains.
- No, they've always been here.

296
00:27:05.880 --> 00:27:10.400
They are sitting at a table and eating
a human being. A captain.

297
00:27:10.480 --> 00:27:12.840
Children too!
- Eating?

298
00:27:13.160 --> 00:27:15.680
Yes, children are eating
their own father.

299
00:27:15.920 --> 00:27:20.120
Father?
- Hello, hello?
